    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1730">

                <pb facs="1400" n="1284" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1284"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 823.124/17.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Lima</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-08-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 15, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The President asks that the Department recommend to serve under Doctor Converse
                    an engineer who has specialized in public water supply and sewerage construction
                    and has had responsible Chargé of such work. He is wanted to supervise the
                    design and construction of works at Iquitos. Preferably member of American
                    Society of Civil Engineers; must be scrupulously honest.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Howard.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
